# sha256 of data/willeq.db, the shipped SQLite database. Rebuilt by
# scripts/build_willeq_db.sh from nine inputs: the EQ client's spells_us.txt,
# eqstr_us.txt, dbstr_us.txt, SoundAssets.txt, AnimationSounds.txt,
# mp3index.txt and eqlsstr_us.txt, plus data/item_models.json and
# config/race_models.json. 28,791 rows across ten tables,
# metadata.version = 7 (kWilleqDbExpectedVersion).
#
# T454 (board B474) dropped the twelfth table, equipment_textures (2,623 rows
# nothing read), and T456 (board B476) dropped the eleventh, equipment_models
# (1,000 rows, nothing read either) -- together the whole of the difference
# from T450's 32,414. The equipment model AND texture paths both resolve LIVE,
# through EquipmentModelLoader::buildEquipmentIndex(); neither table was a
# broken route, both were redundant ones.
#
# metadata.input_digest DID move this time (c39f5cfbb75e5744 ->
# 956f69a5686c98bb), and that is correct: T454 changed only the loader, so the
# nine remaining inputs hashed the same, whereas T456 removed
# data/equipment_models.json from the input set itself. The digest is over the
# inputs, so dropping one must move it.
#
# T450 (board B467) made the file reproducible in the first place: the builder
# used to stamp metadata.build_date = __DATE__ " " __TIME__, so recompiling it
# changed these bytes with identical inputs and no pin was possible. That row
# is now metadata.input_digest, a path-independent digest of the inputs.
#
# Pinned here so an input drift, or a hand-edit of the database, is a ctest
# FAIL (DbReproducible). Update this line in the SAME commit that changes an
# input -- exactly like data/willeq.eqe1.sha256 and data/textures.sha256.
e9fc387f0c3e4d72fb5f3b22fac098917b02006e64d28f784af06d2a8e103ef7  willeq.db
